          "distinct": true,
          "id": "340127b4567e02c66a59e0fdfd3ceeb8b2039874",
          "message": "cuFFT: rework plan construction for efficient non-contiguous batching (#3052)\n\nRewrites the cuFFT plan construction path so that batching dimensions are chosen\ndynamically based on performance, rather than being statically split into leading\n(internal) and trailing (external) batch dims. This fixes catastrophic slowdowns\nwhen transforming along non-innermost dimensions of large arrays (e.g. `fft(x, 2)`\nover a `7×7×1_000_000` array went from ~15s down to ~0.1s, on par with `fft(x, 1)`),\ncaused by launching one kernel per trailing batch slice.\n\nThe rewrite also lifts the previous restriction that transform dimensions had to\nbe given in increasing order for complex FFTs; `plan_fft` / `plan_fft!` now accept\nany permutation, and duplicate dimensions are rejected explicitly instead of being\nsilently deduplicated. `plan_rfft` / `plan_brfft` still require strictly increasing\nregions (since the first entry determines the halved output size), but the error\nis now raised up front with a clear message.\n\nAdditional cleanups on top of the original PR:\n- Out-of-place scratch buffers replace the in-place `circshift!` workaround for\n  R2C/C2R alignment hazards — exception-safe, faster, and no longer mutates user\n  arrays.\n- Half-precision power-of-2 violations now surface as `ArgumentError` at plan\n  construction rather than a bare `CUFFT_INCOMPLETE_PARAMETER_LIST` from deep in\n  the wrapper.\n- `inembed[0]` / `onembed[0]` are padded to satisfy cuFFT's documented `>= n[0]`\n  precondition in the non-contiguous path.\n- Broader test coverage for non-contiguous regions, duplicate-dim rejection, and\n  R2C alignment round-trips.\n\nCo-authored-by: Tim Besard <tim.besard@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-17T13:01:00+02:00",
