          "committer": {
            "email": "noreply@github.com",
            "name": "GitHub",
            "username": "web-flow"
          },
          "distinct": true,
          "id": "e50d7c450e698d1cacc1fb8927742c0e9075059a",
          "message": "Fix misreport of non-SMEM launch failures as SMEM overflow (#3135)\n\n`diagnose_launch_failure` checked dynamic shared-memory size against\n`DEVICE_ATTRIBUTE_MAX_SHARED_MEMORY_PER_BLOCK`, which always returns the\nnon-opt-in 48 KiB ceiling on Volta+. Any kernel that legitimately opted\ninto >48 KiB via `FUNC_ATTRIBUTE_MAX_DYNAMIC_SHARED_SIZE_BYTES` and then\nfailed to launch for an unrelated reason (e.g. register pressure on a\nHopper/Blackwell warp-specialized kernel) was reported as a SMEM overflow,\nhiding the real cause.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-14T09:25:24+02:00",
          "tree_id": "c0d88ed1b1ba54b3479ae78fd80a90634de7859b",
          "url": "https://github.com/JuliaGPU/CUDA.jl/commit/e50d7c450e698d1cacc1fb8927742c0e9075059a"
