          "distinct": true,
          "id": "fcce909a35021f07195e9f63a5b8f3e7972080ee",
          "message": "Rework memory reclamation API; reduce memory usage (#3118)\n\nRework GPU memory reclamation so libraries can release resources under memory pressure instead of pinning them for the lifetime of the owning task. Probing showed CUDA.jl test workers were sitting on ~200 MiB of cuSOLVER workspace each, plus smaller per-library overhead, even after `CUDA.reclaim()`, because finalizers were attached to `current_task()` and the worker tasks never died.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-14T12:39:20+02:00",
          "tree_id": "1bca909d83c4ad3d2d0f524b0ec07c5fbf8357b1",
