          "distinct": true,
          "id": "2de761e725a6d8a8693f9c2164ea73e9bfc353b5",
          "message": "cuSPARSE: Implement dense * COO matmul without prior sorting (#3005)\n\nThe current implementation of `mm!` of a dense and a sparse matrix\n(with a COO matrix as the second argument) required users to sort the\nCOO matrix before multiplication, otherwise it would silently return\nincorrect results (see issue #2820). Sorting required copying the whole\nmatrix.\n\nThis rewrites the dense × sparse path: CSC/CSR cases are dispatched by\nre-viewing the sparse operand under the opposite format with reversed\ndims (a zero-copy transpose), then routed through the sparse × dense\n`mm!` using `transpose(A)`/`transpose(C)`. The COO case keeps the\noriginal matrix but flips `transb` to realise the transpose, except for\ncomplex × `'C'`, which has no \"conjugate-only\" cuSPARSE flag and so\nmaterialises `conj.(B.nzVal)` (values only — much cheaper than a full\nsort).\n\nThe sparse × dense `mm!` signature now accepts\n`Union{DenseCuMatrix, Transpose{<:Any, <:DenseCuMatrix}}` for B and C,\nbacked by a new `CuDenseMatrixDescriptor(::Transpose{...})` helper.\n\nAlso removes `mm_wrapper`, which only duplicated the size checks in\n`mm!` and shortcut on `isempty(B)` to return a fresh zero matrix of the\nwrong shape rather than writing into `C`. Tests are extended to cover\ntransposed dense inputs/outputs on the sparse × dense path and to drop\nthe prior `sort_coo` requirement on the dense × sparse COO path; the\nCSR_ALG3 algorithm guards are tightened to match cuSPARSE 12.5.8/12.6.3.",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-15T13:46:40+02:00",
          "tree_id": "433b027d25ee5c3d0db4674847b71710e97ebd2f",
          "url": "https://github.com/JuliaGPU/CUDA.jl/commit/2de761e725a6d8a8693f9c2164ea73e9bfc353b5"
