          "distinct": true,
          "id": "0ad0204a2e4b65dfaae6d699deb978e2247226cb",
          "message": "Expose directed-rounding floating-point intrinsics (#2576)\n\nAdd `add_{rn,rz,rm,rp}`, `mul_*`, `div_*`, `fma_*` for Float32 and\nFloat64, mapping directly to the NVPTX `{add,mul,div,fma}.<rnd>.{f32,f64}`\ninstructions. `sub_*` is implemented via `add_*(x, -y)` since NVPTX lacks a\ndedicated rounded-sub intrinsic and float negation is bit-exact.\n\nCo-authored-by: Tim Besard <tim@juliahub.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-15T16:13:08+02:00",
          "tree_id": "27e25f93350a87a8bfe9814aff12b2725805a06d",
          "url": "https://github.com/JuliaGPU/CUDA.jl/commit/0ad0204a2e4b65dfaae6d699deb978e2247226cb"
