          "distinct": true,
          "id": "2fe75d66ff3dd222e8189315f4c966f6153271e0",
          "message": "Reduce usage of `libdevice`, relying more on LLVM (#3149)\n\nBuilding on https://github.com/JuliaGPU/GPUCompiler.jl/pull/805, https://github.com/JuliaGPU/GPUCompiler.jl/pull/804, https://github.com/JuliaGPU/GPUCompiler.jl/pull/800, avoid some of the uses of `libdevice`'s intrinsics, instead emitting vanilla LLVM IR and having GPUCompiler.jl post-process it into what we need in PTX. This has many advantages, including (potentially) better optimization, compatibility with LLVM tools like Enzyme, etc.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-21T13:18:49+02:00",
          "tree_id": "f50d2a2c7f75bf0d4669a05f075ec5b4c7bb7976",
